    "agent_messages": [
      "I've added `POST /purchases/{id}/countersign`. It builds and `go test ./...` passes, but no package has test files and there were no database credentials, so I haven't run it against a real database.\n\n**What changed (only in `internal/candidate`):**\n- **`operations.go`:** a new `countersignOp` operation named `countersign.v6` for the approver role. It moves a purchase from `pending-second` to `approved`, only for purchases other people created. It requires a different approver from the one who did the first approval, and the submitted amount must equal the purchase's current amount. It writes the outbox event `purchase.countersigned`, which the `notify` package already handles.\n- **`approval.go`:** the new route is registered with `protocol.Confirm(\"countersign\", \"approver\", …)` in front of the existing reopen, bulk-approve and bulk-reject routes, which are unchanged. Errors from the action kernel are turned into protocol errors the same way the other endpoints do it.\n\n**What the kernel already covers:** the role check (403/401 come from the shared adapter), tenant and ownership checks, and returning 409 for a wrong amount or a target that doesn't qualify. It also handles locking per idempotency key, and writes the status change, audit row, event and `ActionRequest` row in one transaction. If the `ActionRequest` insert fails, the whole transaction rolls back and the request returns 503. Once a purchase is approved it is no longer in `submitted` or `pending-second`, so bulk-approve, bulk-reject and countersign all refuse it. The database trigger also enforces this.\n\n**One addition beyond the kernel:** the kernel's replay check only looks at the purchase ID, not the amount. So a repeat with the same key but a different amount would otherwise come back as a successful replay. I added a small read-only check, used only on replays, that compares the amount against the purchase and returns 409 if they differ. This is safe because the app's database role can't change `amount`."
    ],
